---
config:
  flowchart:
    nodeSpacing: 24
---
flowchart TB
    accTitle: The way of a pull request into main
    accDescr: You open a pull request. The title check and the labeler give it the labels of its type and its areas, and the 15 required checks run. After they finish, the flaky-test bot runs a failed job once more, the cancelled-check bot restarts a run that a late run cancelled, and the coverage bot comments with the coverage against main; a job that runs again goes back to the checks. Once every check passes, the pull request merges if it is up to date with main; otherwise the branch bot updates its branch and the checks run again. It is then squashed into main. You are orange, the bots blue, and main green.

    pr(["You open a<br>pull request"])
    labels["Title check<br>and labeler:<br>type and area<br>labels"]
    checks{"15 required<br>checks"}
    after["After the checks:<br>flaky-test bot,<br>coverage bot,<br>cancelled-check bot"]
    current{"Up to date<br>with main?"}
    branch["Branch bot:<br>updates the<br>branch"]
    main(["Squashed<br>into main"])

    pr --> labels --> checks
    checks -- "finished" --> after
    after -. "a failed or<br>cancelled job<br>runs again" .-> checks
    checks -- "every check<br>passes" --> current
    current -- "no" --> branch
    branch -- "the checks<br>run again" --> checks
    current -- "yes" --> main

    classDef yours fill:#f59e0b2e,stroke:#f59e0b,stroke-width:2px
    classDef bots fill:#526cfe2e,stroke:#526cfe,stroke-width:2px
    classDef result fill:#16a34a2e,stroke:#16a34a,stroke-width:2px
    class pr yours
    class labels,checks,after,current,branch bots
    class main result
